    {
        "content": "<p>I suspect it's asking about something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Isabelle\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kp\">shows</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"foo\"</span>\n<span class=\"kp\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span>\n<span class=\"k\">proof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span>\n<span class=\"ow\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>vs</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Isabelle\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kp\">shows</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"foo\"</span>\n<span class=\"k\">proof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span>\n<span class=\"ow\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(and variations)</p>\n<p>my answer: there isn't really a difference, it's a bit a matter of style, I think</p>",
        "id": 640333498,
        "sender_full_name": "Yong Kiam",
        "timestamp": 1794670438
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If that is the question, see also <a href=\"https://proofcraft.org/blog/isabelle-style.html\">https://proofcraft.org/blog/isabelle-style.html</a> for why this is a bad idea in general (and <a href=\"https://proofcraft.org/blog/isabelle-style-part2.html\">https://proofcraft.org/blog/isabelle-style-part2.html</a>)</p>\n<p>EDIT: I misremembered and it is in the first part</p>",
